---
// Why no engine computes the product: sizes at the lab's scale on a log axis, then a real
// measurement of a join that can use equality against one that cannot.
const sizes = [
  { label: 'customer', n: 150_000, tone: 'build' },
  { label: 'orders', n: 1_500_000, tone: 'build' },
  { label: 'customer × orders', n: 225_000_000_000, tone: 'warn' },
  { label: 'customer ⋈ orders (on id)', n: 1_500_000, tone: 'probe' },
];
const maxExp = 12; // axis runs from 10^0 to 10^12
const pos = (n: number) => (Math.log10(n) / maxExp) * 100;
const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');

// Measured by lab/crates/m01-relational/examples/joins.rs on a 2-core cloud VM, 15 warm runs.
const timings = [
  { label: 'ON a.k = b.k: hash join', ms: 1.189 },
  { label: 'ON a.k + b.k = 5001: nested loop', ms: 39.974 },
  { label: 'ON b.k = 5001 - a.k: hash join', ms: 1.384 },
];
const maxMs = Math.max(...timings.map((t) => t.ms));
---

<figure class="qe-ps not-content">
  <p class="title">Rows at the lab’s scale, logarithmic axis</p>
  <ul class="bars">
    {
      sizes.map((s) => (
        <li>
          <span class="k">{s.label}</span>
          <span class="track">
            <span class={`fill ${s.tone}`} style={`width:${pos(s.n)}%`} />
          </span>
          <span class="v">{fmt(s.n)}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p class="axis">
    Bar lengths are logarithmic: each extra twelfth of the width means ten times more rows. The product’s bar looks
    under twice as long as the join’s, yet it is 150,000 times larger.
  </p>

  <p class="title second">Same 5,000 output rows from two 5,000-row tables, median of 15 runs</p>
  <ul class="bars linear">
    {
      timings.map((t, i) => (
        <li>
          <span class="k">{t.label}</span>
          <span class="track">
            <span class={`fill ${i === 1 ? 'warn' : 'probe'}`} style={`width:${Math.max(1.5, (t.ms / maxMs) * 100)}%`} />
          </span>
          <span class="v">{t.ms.toFixed(1)} ms</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <figcaption>
    Measured with DataFusion 55.2 by the lab’s <code>joins</code> example on a 2-core cloud VM. An equality between the
    two sides lets the engine build a hash table and look up only matching rows. The expression
    <code>a.k + b.k = 5001</code> mixes both sides, so the engine tests all 25 million pairs. The same condition,
    rearranged so each side uses one table, gets a hash join again. Times are from one machine; the roughly 30× gap is
    what matters.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .qe-ps {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
  }
  .title {
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .title.second {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }
  .bars {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .bars li {
    margin: 0 !important;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    grid-template-areas: 'k v' 't t';
    gap: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
  }
  .k { grid-area: k; font-family: var(--sl-font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; }
  .v {
    grid-area: v;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .track {
    grid-area: t;
    height: 0.85rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--sl-color-black);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .fill.build { background: var(--qe-pipe-build); }
  .fill.probe { background: var(--sl-color-accent); }
  .fill.warn { background: var(--qe-warn); }
  .axis {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
  figcaption code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  @media (max-width: 49.99rem) {
    .qe-ps {
      margin-inline: var(--qe-bleed);
      border-radius: 0;
      border-inline: 0;
      padding: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
